{#
  A chart canvas and nothing else.

  The spec goes out as a data attribute and admin.js builds the Chart from it,
  so colours are resolved from CSS custom properties at render time. The old
  dashboard-chart template shipped a full Chart.js options object per chart from
  PHP with `rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05)` grid lines baked in, which is why dark mode
  could never be fixed in the stylesheet: the wrong colour was in the JSON.

  Datasets name a semantic `role` (accent, info, success, warning, danger,
  muted); the client turns that into the theme's actual colour.
#}
<div class="dash-chart" style="height: {{ height|default(280) }}px">
  <canvas data-chart="{{ chart|json_encode|e('html_attr') }}"></canvas>
</div>
